Revision history for static

{{$NEXT}}
  - Reject reachable return/return-rw without an enclosing Routine, including
    eager collection callbacks at unit scope.
  - Analyze finite callback batches, optional arguments and Slip results, plus
    reduce/classify/categorize, rotor, zip/cross and dynamic selection counts.
  - Infer loop elements and bounded state, empty/repeat/infinite paths and
    last/next exits; preserve conservative widening for unknown loops.
  - Resolve finite callable/computed-method alternatives and local FALLBACK;
    reuse compiler-created custom generic witnesses without executing providers.
  - Invalidate nested tracked aliases, propagate eager callback effects and
    nonlocal returns, and retain lazy callback exception summaries.
  - Model Failure returns and known CONTROL/resume/rethrow paths; extend bounded
    primitive string, numeric, collection and interval predicate rules.
  - Report unreachable code by default with policy-dependent warning/failure,
    with :check-unreachable and --/check-unreachable opt-out.
  - Refine constant/type/definedness branches, short-circuit paths and integer
    intervals; evaluate predicates using earlier parameter bindings.
  - Analyze CORE collection callbacks, counted pick/roll and pop/shift state.
  - Resolve known indirect calls, finite captures and nested CORE generic contracts.
  - Track normal returns, explicit throws and termination separately, propagate
    local exception summaries and preserve deferred Promise exceptions.

0.0.1  2026-10-22T01:08:37+01:00
  - Disable Mi6 README generation from Pod to preserve the maintained README.md.
  - Hide the warning emission callback from diagnostic backtraces.
  - Infer possible element returns of no-argument CORE pick/roll on built-in lists/arrays.
  - Check each inferred body return alternative against declared return contracts.
  - Add opt-in CHECK-time RakuAST type analysis of the current compilation unit.
  - Add warning/failure policies for mismatches and inconclusive checks.
  - Infer local routine returns with .are and bounded recursive summaries.
  - Check assignments, calls, methods, multis, returns and typed collections.
  - Report fatal diagnostics as native compilation errors at the offending expression.
  - Analyze bounded pure where/subset predicates using propagated constants.
  - Bind direct generic captures, rank nominal multi candidates and check hash keys.
  - Track native integer storage, lexical aliases and conservative mutation effects.
  - Expand policy, signature, primitive type, dynamic syntax and safety coverage.
  - Check missing methods on exact invocants by default; add :check-methods option.
  - Add bin/static-check.raku for compile-only validation of files or stdin,
    with selectable policies and the existing checker options.
  - Accept repeatable -I/-M CLI options and forward interpreter repositories.
  - Validate readonly/rw parameter contracts, finite destructuring and fixed
    array dimensions, with lexical and element binding checks.
  - Analyze given/when paths, exception handlers, deferred producer payloads,
    supply callback contracts and finite hyper operations conservatively.
